{
  "id": "m13-b1",
  "title": "Swarm Sum",
  "difficulty": "easy",
  "story": "The swarm's first job: add up a long list of cargo weights, split across **4** drone threads.\n\nInput: `n` (0–100000), then n whole numbers, each between -1000000000 and 1000000000.\n\nOutput: their total.\n\nSplit the list into 4 slices, let each thread add up its own slice, then combine the four results after joining.",
  "starter": "#include <stdio.h>\n#include <stdlib.h>\n#include <pthread.h>\n\n#define DRONES 4\n\ntypedef struct {\n    const int *values;\n    int from, to;   // values[from] .. values[to - 1]\n    long long sum;\n} Job;\n\nint main(void) {\n    int n;\n    scanf(\"%d\", &n);\n    int *values = malloc((n > 0 ? n : 1) * sizeof(int));\n    if (values == NULL) return 1;\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) scanf(\"%d\", &values[i]);\n\n    // split the work across DRONES threads, then print the total\n\n    free(values);\n    return 0;\n}\n",
  "compileFlags": "-pthread",
