  "hints": [
    "Each thread gets a Job: `from`, `to` and its own `sum`. The thread function loops `for (int i = job->from; i < job->to; i++) job->sum += job->values[i];`.",
    "Split like the lesson: `base = n / DRONES`, `extra = n % DRONES`, and the first `extra` threads get one more. With n smaller than 4, some threads get an empty slice: that's fine, their sum stays 0.",
    "Three numbers of 1000000000 already overflow an int, so the sums are `long long`: print with `%lld`. Join all four threads before adding up their sums."
  ],
  "solution": "#include <stdio.h>\n#include <stdlib.h>\n#include <pthread.h>\n\n#define DRONES 4\n\ntypedef struct {\n    const int *values;\n    int from, to;\n    long long sum;\n} Job;\n\nvoid *add_slice(void *arg) {\n    Job *job = arg;\n    for (int i = job->from; i < job->to; i++) job->sum += job->values[i];\n    return NULL;\n}\n\nint main(void) {\n    int n;\n    scanf(\"%d\", &n);\n    int *values = malloc((n > 0 ? n : 1) * sizeof(int));\n    if (values == NULL) return 1;\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) scanf(\"%d\", &values[i]);\n\n    pthread_t threads[DRONES];\n    Job jobs[DRONES];\n    int base = n / DRONES, extra = n % DRONES, next = 0;\n    for (int i = 0; i < DRONES; i++) {\n        int size = base + (i < extra ? 1 : 0);\n        jobs[i] = (Job){ values, next, next + size, 0 };\n        next += size;\n        pthread_create(&threads[i], NULL, add_slice, &jobs[i]);\n    }\n    long long total = 0;\n    for (int i = 0; i < DRONES; i++) {\n        pthread_join(threads[i], NULL);\n        total += jobs[i].sum;\n    }\n    printf(\"%lld\\n\", total);\n    free(values);\n    return 0;\n}\n"
}
